+# PiBoy DMG / Wayland: restore the pre-launch configure menu.
+#
+# Under a compositor this script has no controlling terminal, which breaks the
+# menu two ways at once: the key read gets EOF instead of a keypress, and dialog
+# would draw onto the VT that labwc is covering, so it would be invisible even
+# if it could be reached. Re-exec the whole script inside a Wayland terminal,
+# which supplies a pty - /dev/tty becomes a real device, the key read works, and
+# the menu is visible. The emulator then opens its own Wayland window on top,
+# and the terminal closes when it exits.
+#
+# The terminal itself is opened by foot-run.sh, so the flags that make dialog
+# usable here (--term, because foot's own terminfo is not installed) live in one
+# file this project owns rather than in a patch against a third-party script.
+#
+# The guards stay HERE, though, and are not delegated: foot-run.sh refuses with
+# exit 2 when it cannot get a terminal, which is right for the configuration
+# menu but wrong for this script - a game must still launch without one. So the
+# conditions are tested up front and we simply fall through when any of them
+# fails, into the TTY_IN safety net further down. RUNCOMMAND_IN_TERM stops the
+# re-exec recursing; on a KMS boot /dev/tty is real and none of this runs.
+#
+# Reapply from piboy-dmg/patches/runcommand-wayland.patch after a
+# RetroPie-Setup update.
+FOOT_RUN="/opt/retropie/configs/all/wayland/foot-run.sh"
+if [[ -n "$WAYLAND_DISPLAY" && -z "$RUNCOMMAND_IN_TERM" ]] \
+   && ! { : </dev/tty; } 2>/dev/null \
+   && command -v foot >/dev/null && [[ -x "$FOOT_RUN" ]]; then
+    export RUNCOMMAND_IN_TERM=1
+    exec "$FOOT_RUN" "$0" "$@"
+fi
+
 ROOTDIR="/opt/retropie"
 CONFIGDIR="$ROOTDIR/configs"
 LOG="/dev/shm/runcommand.log"
