+# PiBoy DMG / Wayland: under a compositor there is no controlling terminal.
+# labwc detaches from the VT, so EmulationStation runs with tty "?" and every
+# child inherits that - opening /dev/tty then fails with ENXIO. That breaks two
+# things below: the "press a button to configure" key read, and, fatally, the
+# emulator launch itself, which redirects stdin from /dev/tty. With no fallback
+# nothing launches at all under Wayland.
+#
+# This is now only the SAFETY NET. The block near the top of this script
+# re-execs into a Wayland terminal when one is available, which supplies a pty
+# and makes /dev/tty real - so the pre-launch menu works normally under Wayland
+# (verified: visible, readable, and navigable with the d-pad via joy2key).
+# TTY_IN only falls back to /dev/null if that re-exec did not happen, e.g. foot
+# is not installed; games then still launch, just with no configure menu.
+# Under a normal KMS boot /dev/tty is present and behaviour is unchanged.
+#
+# Only the INPUT redirections are routed through TTY_IN. The seven remaining
+# `>/dev/tty` output redirections are all inside main_menu, choose_mode,
+# choose_emulator, choose_render_res and user_menu - reached only after
+# check_menu sees a keypress. In the fallback path check_menu reads from
+# /dev/null, gets EOF immediately, and none of them is reachable; in the foot
+# path /dev/tty is a real pty and they work as written. So they need no
+# fallback, and giving them one would only add a way to write a menu to
+# /dev/null. Re-check this if check_menu ever gains another caller.
+#
+# Reapply from piboy-dmg/patches/runcommand-wayland.patch after a
+# RetroPie-Setup update.
+if { : </dev/tty; } 2>/dev/null; then
+    TTY_IN="/dev/tty"
+else
+    TTY_IN="/dev/null"
+fi
+
 function check_menu() {
     local dont_launch=0
     # check for key pressed to enter configuration
-    IFS= read -s -t 2 -N 1 key </dev/tty
+    IFS= read -s -t 2 -N 1 key <"$TTY_IN"
     if [[ -n "$key" ]]; then
         [[ -n "$IMG_PID" ]] && kill -SIGINT "$IMG_PID"
         tput cnorm
@@ -1300,7 +1363,7 @@
